13. LOGIC FLOW
Purchase Flow (Engineering Format)
START
    ↓
1. User clicks "Buy Prompt 4"
    ↓
2. Frontend: POST /api/create-checkout {email, promptId: 4}
    ↓
3. Backend: Create Stripe Checkout Session
    ↓
4. Backend: Return {checkoutUrl}
    ↓
5. Frontend: Redirect to Stripe Checkout
    ↓
6. User enters card + completes payment
    ↓
7. Stripe: Fire webhook → POST /api/webhook/stripe
    ↓
8. Backend: Verify webhook signature
    ↓
9. Backend: Store purchase in KV
    KEY: `purchase:alex@example.com:4`
    VALUE: {purchaseDate, price, sessionId}
    ↓
10. Backend: Send email via Resend
    Subject: "You've unlocked Prompt 4!"
    Body: "Click here: /auth?token=XXX"
    ↓
11. Stripe: Redirect user to /unlock?email=XXX&prompt=4
    ↓
12. Frontend: GET /api/prompt/4?email=XXX
    ↓
13. Backend: Check KV for purchase:alex@example.com:4
    ↓
14. IF EXISTS → Return prompt content
    ELSE → Return 403 Forbidden
    ↓
15. Frontend: Display prompt + Copy button
    ↓
END

Auth Flow (Magic Link)
START
    ↓
1. User enters email on /dashboard
    ↓
2. Frontend: POST /api/send-magic-link {email}
    ↓
3. Backend: Generate JWT token (expires 24h)
    payload: {email, exp, jti}
    ↓
4. Backend: Send email with link /auth?token=XXX
    ↓
5. User clicks link
    ↓
6. Frontend: GET /api/verify-token?token=XXX
    ↓
7. Backend: Verify JWT signature + expiration
    ↓
8. IF VALID → Burn token (mark as used in KV)
              → Return {email, purchases}
              → Set session cookie (30 days)
    ELSE → Return 401 Unauthorized
    ↓
9. Frontend: Store session in localStorage
    ↓
10. Redirect to /dashboard
    ↓
END


